# Smart Mirror Pi — environment variable reference
#
# The application reads all runtime configuration from config/settings.json,
# not from environment variables.  The variables below are shell-level hints
# consumed by scripts/run.sh (and the systemd unit) — not Python os.environ.
#
# Copy this file to .env and adjust as needed, then source it before running
# manually:
#   source .env && scripts/run.sh
#
# The systemd unit sets these via Environment= directives in the [Service]
# section, so .env is only needed for manual / ad-hoc runs.

# ── Qt display backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Overrides the auto-detection in run.sh.
# Values: wayland | xcb | eglfs
# Default: auto-detected from WAYLAND_DISPLAY / DISPLAY environment.
# QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland

# ── Qt Multimedia backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Force a specific Qt multimedia backend.
# Values: gstreamer | ffmpeg
# Default: gstreamer (required on Raspberry Pi; FFmpeg stalls on Pi hardware)
# QT_MEDIA_BACKEND=gstreamer

# ── GStreamer (Wayland) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GL windowing system used by GStreamer under Wayland.
# Default: wayland (auto-set by run.sh when QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland)
# GST_GL_WINDOW=wayland
# GST_GL_PLATFORM=egl

# ── GStreamer codec priority ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Demote the Pi hardware H264 decoder (v4l2h264dec) to avoid crashes on
# -tune zerolatency streams; prefer avdec_h264 (software, libavcodec).
# Default set by run.sh — uncomment only to override.
# GST_PLUGIN_FEATURE_RANK=avdec_h264:256,v4l2h264dec:50

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ensures stdout/stderr are not buffered (set automatically by run.sh).
# PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1

# ── Display server (Pi / headless) ───────────────────────────────────────
# These are normally set by the graphical session; set them manually only
# when running without a display manager (e.g. bare systemd service).
# WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-0
# DISPLAY=:0
